CORE
shapes.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member names in default member initializers: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.id.general]/4, [expr.unary.op]/4: in a default member
initializer, of a class with or without a user-provided constructor, `x'
is `(*this).x', so `&x' and the parenthesized `&(s::x)' are `int *'; the
qualified `&s::y' forms a pointer to member, also in a member function
where `this' exists (on bin53 that was `int *': "invalid implicit
conversion from 'signed int *' to 'signed int (struct s:: *)'").  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept the program.
